  "Design Code"
]]]></Value>
    </codeType>
    <description>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "blocks": {
    "contentData": [],
    "settingsData": [],
    "expose": [],
    "Layout": {}
  },
  "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EProposed street designs \u003Cstrong\u003Emust \u003C/strong\u003Emaintain a cohesive and positive design language throughout the development to ensure legibility and create a clear, recognisable street network. \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EApplicants \u003Cstrong\u003Emust \u003C/strong\u003Ereference the Local Character and Contextual Assessment (C1.2 and G1.2 as relevant) when selecting materials, colours, and styles for pathways, signage, and landscaping to reinforce local identity and enhance wayfinding. \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EExceptions:\u003C/strong\u003E \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u2022 in major developments, it may be appropriate to include a variety of street design palettes which align with proposed character areas to help establish distinct\u0026nbsp;neighbourhood identities and support intuitive wayfinding through visual cues, while maintaining an overall sense of cohesion \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u2022 deviations from local materials, colours, or styles may be acceptable if the proposed alternatives demonstrate higher quality or make a positive contribution to the area\u2019s character\u003C/p\u003E"
}]]></Value>
    </description>
    <developmentScales>
      <Value><![CDATA[[
  "Minor Residential Applications (1-9 homes)",
  "Major Residential Applications (10\u002B homes)",
  "Minor Employment Applications",
  "Major Employment Applications",
  "Other Major Applications"
]]]></Value>
    </developmentScales>
